    "summary": "gather.relationCall for quality and adherence: a cut 'calls' relation is judged once (both full rows when they fit, else one full row against the other's summary in each direction, each measured; a row that cannot fit is named, never cut). A relation finding must be at the caller: rows carry no line ranges, so the prompt asks for the caller's file AND its name in the message, and gather.validate rejects anything else (fixed-size reasons; re-issued once, then the review fails). New test: a real contract disagreement (fill may return undefined, placeOrder reads .total unchecked) cut across chunks; a reviewer judging only from what each call carries finds it only in the relation call the job issues, and the finding lands at the caller.",
